WEBVTT

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.120
Hey, about Eiji-san's body...

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.170
Yeah.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.670
I can't stand it anymore.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.920
What the hell are you doing?

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.120
Boss...

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.180
Eiji's body smells so nice.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.480
Such a sweet smell...

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.390
We're on a diet, and it's unbearable.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.390
Gosh, I want to eat him up.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.150
It was something like that.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.870
I guess since I'm not a boxer anymore,

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.780
I shouldn't stay here.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.530
Well...

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.200
After I finish this, I'll gather my things, boss.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.510
Eiji.

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:43.270
So are you going to move, Kanda-kun?

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:46.770
Well, you can call it that, but I don't have a lot of stuff.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.270
Are you all right?

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.330
Eh? What do you mean?

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:53.730
Wouldn't it be better to tell Tachibana, just in case?

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:57.070
He might give you some support.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.340
It's fine.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.030
Besides, I'm still a apprentice.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.000
You guys, there's big news!

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.950
Odaiba TV is coming here.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.860
Odaiba TV?

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.540
What's that?

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.970
So, Ooshima-ana,

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.670
what's on "Handy Info For The Housewife" next week?

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.610
All right!

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:22.490
It's a special program on a limited-duration cake fair at a department store food court.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.290
That sounds interesting.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:28.790
We'll be showing a lot of fine sweets, and they're all very popular.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.640
We hope everyone will watch it.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.200
That's what I'm talking about.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:36.020
The "Super Super News" is coming here to talk to us.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.980
Why are you so happy?

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:41.050
Young master likes those female announcers.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.290
Yes, that's right.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:44.800
No, that's not what I meant at all!

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.240
It will be great advertising if the program features us.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.250
B-But, what's this about a cake fair at a department store food court?

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:56.050
It's a great chance to let people know about our cakes.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:59.420
We'll sell cakes in the food court on a temporary basis.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.970
So I'm counting on you guys.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:14.620
I'm Nakatsu Haruka, an announcer from Odaiba TV.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.980
I'm Ooshima Yukari.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.410
Pleased to meet you.
Pleased to meet you.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.690
Nice to meet you.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.160
I'm Tachibana, the owner of this shop.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.820
This is our pâtissier...

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.410
I'm Ono.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:29.330
This is a nice shop.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.830
Well, I retained an antique motif for all the interior decoration and tableware.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.790
And everyone is cool.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.080
I'm sorry to get straight to the main subject,

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.050
but have you already decided your menu for the food court?

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.460
Yes.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.470
Now, please take a seat.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:54.920
Well, we would like everyone to enjoy gorgeous desserts that could be viewed as the pinnacle of French cuisine.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.190
Damn, she's got a nice pair.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:01.230
How scary, they're like melons.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:05.360
Could you tell us which of your superb cakes you'd recommend?

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.950
Certainly.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.390
Then could you prepare it?

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:10.970
Yes.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.390
Yeah.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:22.610
Done.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:23.340
Yes.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.180
This Cassis is what we recommend.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:32.850
The combination of a fig's crackly texture and the light taste of Cassis mousse

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.060
is our recommendation for this season.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:38.160
Then we'll try it.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:49.330
Why do women dance around when they eat something delicious?

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.490
You do too, on occasion.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.070
This is really tasty!

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:58.060
This might not be the right way to describe this cake,

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:00.880
but it somehow tastes very sexy.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.270
I apologize.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:10.280
He's embarrassed to be praised by a beautiful woman.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:11.070
Oh!

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.180
Really?

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.930
Liar.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:22.030
Sensei, are you all right?

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.510
You look pale.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.560
I'm really scared...

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.280
of women.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.070
You idiot.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:32.250
The customers at department stores are mostly women.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.640
But...

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:38.110
after I realized I was gay and tried various ways of playing,

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.080
I suddenly had trouble dealing with women.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:43.290
Ways of playing?

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.340
Umm... no!

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.200
Anyway, I'll do my best.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.070
Yeah, I'm counting on you.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:51.230
The actual fair is this weekend.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:55.090
And our shop would be closed tomorrow anyway, so we'll go look over the terrain.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.350
Then, bye-bye.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.960
Geez.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:01.400
Gramps is rushing headlong by himself.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.820
Are you really all right?

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:06.510
Well, somehow.

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:12.910
Tachibana must have had something in mind when he decided to open this shop.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:17.480
I think I was in the fourth grade.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.660
My mom was watching TV with me and said,

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:27.130
"Oh, poor child. That kidnapped boy, Keiichirou-kun, is the same age as you.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:31.170
Since it's been two weeks already, he's not likely to be rescued."

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:39.310
So when Tachibana was rescued, we were glad,

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:43.190
but I guess matters got tougher after that,

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:46.560
for Tachibana and his family.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.140
By the way,

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:51.990
Kanda-kun, you didn't tell him you're moving.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.240
Well, it will work out somehow.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.280
But where are you going to stay?

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.290
I'm really fine.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.050
Oh, I have to clean up.

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:14.160
I remember one thing about the man who kidnapped me.

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:20.060
He liked cake, and every day he forced me to eat the cake he bought.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:25.810
Gramps has his own dark emptiness that I know nothing about.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:28.350
I must do my best.

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:44.720
Sorry for making you come in on your day off.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:47.710
We're going now to the department store to prepare for the fair!

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:48.780
Yay!

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:49.670
Yes!

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:52.130
By the way, while the fair is in progress,

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.680
Ono and I will be at the department store.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.890
So I'll leave this place to Eiji and Chikage.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.470
A-Are you serious?

00:08:58.470 --> 00:08:59.680
I'm very anxious.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:00.850
Me too.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:02.710
I'm anxious too...

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:07.650
The customers at department stores are mostly women.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.690
Come on, cheer up, you guys!

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.190
Okay now, let's go!

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.000
Okay!

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:13.400
Yes!

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:30.170
Wow.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:33.300
Now, where is our booth?

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:38.590
Hey.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:39.140
Huh?

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:40.690
He's here.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:41.970
Is that Ono?

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:43.680
It's him.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.610
I don't know why, but aren't we getting a lot of attention?

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:50.520
More to the point, I think it's hostility.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.530
Move.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.320
Stop standing in the middle of the aisle.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:57.820
What?!

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.450
Stop it, Nakai.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.760
Our shop had a hard time because of this faggot.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.370
I can't stand just remaining silent.

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:08.840
You bastard!

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.620
Sensei isn't a faggot.

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:11.650
Gay! He's gay!

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.380
Could you stop that, Kanda-kun?

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:17.580
It's true that I'm considered a nuisance in this industry.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:18.630
How can you say that?

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:22.180
It's in the past.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:23.420
Don't worry about it!

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:24.470
Hey, let's go.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.600
It's going to be tough here too.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:34.440
Yes.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:39.830
Hey, Tachibana.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:43.090
The kitchen is visible from the outside.

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:46.240
Yeah. We demonstrate and sell. It's quite popular in food courts.

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:49.960
You can show your artistry to our customers.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.680
No... I can't.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:56.090
How can I make desserts while surrounded by women?

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.900
Don't worry.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:01.340
Watch the splendid way I handle the women who are rushing for your cakes.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:02.320
Really?

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.600
Yeah, you can count on me!

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:06.430
Sorry.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:08.520
I got a sty in my eye.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:10.360
Eh?

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.600
Then who's going to serve the customers at the fair?

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:14.810
Umm... I-I'll do it.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.430
But I don't think I'll be that helpful.

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:19.840
I'll apologize for that first.

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:31.350
Okay.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:36.220
I wonder if the team at the department store is all right.

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:38.600
Well, I suppose it'll work out somehow.

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:39.580
What?

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.510
This is weird.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.500
Why won't they mix?

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:44.180
What?

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:48.660
What's going on?!

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.010
It's separating!

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:50.640
Huh?

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:53.560
I'm following sensei's recipe,

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:55.650
but the Cassis mousse is separating!

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.110
You idiot!

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.270
Call Ono on his cell phone.

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:03.700
But sensei's probably busy right now.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.610
Then what are you going to do?

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:07.210
It's time to open the shop.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.060
I'll try it again!

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.050
Welcome.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:31.710
So, we're here at the food court cake fair!

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:32.990
Look at this.

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:37.310
It just opened, but the hall is already packed with customers.

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:43.470
What should I do, Chikage-san?

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:45.830
I really can't do this.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:48.160
I can't give a cooking demonstration in front of women.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:50.160
I can't serve either,

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.040
since I get nervous so quickly.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.970
How can I serve with my sunglasses off?

00:12:56.750 --> 00:13:01.350
I'm sorry, but we can't have you serve our customers wearing sunglasses.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:03.580
Could you take them off?

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.350
Chikage-san.

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.810
Since the fair has started, let's resolve to do this.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.280
Yes.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:17.150
Become someone else.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.280
Yes.

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:19.340
Wait a sec.

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:22.480
Excuse me, could you let me through?

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.070
Excuse me.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:27.610
Oh!

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:29.720
Excuse me.

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:32.220
Could you lend me your earrings?

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:32.790
Eh?

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:34.750
Please.

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:40.910
It's no good! It doesn't work at all!

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:42.570
There's no choice.

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:44.840
Go ask Ono directly.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.090
The Cassis doesn't need to be ready before opening.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.390
No, I can't do that!

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:53.390
Cassis is the most popular item this season.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:58.340
If I was a customer and found that the cake I wanted wasn't there, I'd be angry.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.560
But...

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:05.050
I can't betray sensei's confidence while he's not here!

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:07.630
Could you let me try again?!

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:08.490
Please, gramps!

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:15.150
Look, look.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:17.830
He seems like a different person.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:27.850
Now, Chikage-san.

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:30.470
I'll take Tachibana's place for today.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:32.100
Ono-san...

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:41.860
Hey, Eiji.

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:48.610
Didn't Ono say that it would be better if the puree is colder than the fresh cream, or something like that?

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.320
That's it!

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:59.150
Now, Antique is open.

00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:01.730
I want to see how the customers react.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.380
Hey, could you...

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:05.600
Yes?

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:08.630
What does this Choux Gorgonzola taste like?

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:09.840
That is...

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:11.220
Chikage-san,

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:14.420
if the customers ask you something,

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:17.430
look into their eyes and say...

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:20.610
You will know after you have it.

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:23.020
Th-Then I'll take it.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.540
Wh-What about this Compote de Poire?

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.020
You will know after you have it.

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:31.350
I-I'll take one.

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:32.760
Certainly.

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:36.350
Ono-san, I did it!

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:39.590
I did as you said, and it turned out all right.

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:40.620
See?

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:57.510
Yes!

00:15:58.310 --> 00:15:59.300
Is it done?

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:00.170
Yeah.

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:02.390
I'll unmold it right away.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:08.820
We made it just in time.

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:11.650
Yeah.

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:16.660
Here you are.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.060
Looks nice!

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.090
He's served the desserts.

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:22.870
Let's ask how it tastes.

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:27.350
Young lady, how did it taste?

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:29.630
Mmmmm...
Mmmmm...

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:35.150
As you can see, they're dancing because of the taste.

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:38.350
You could say it's a taste that makes people dance spontaneously.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:40.470
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:42.810
Here is your Cassis.

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:48.290
Thank you very much.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.550
So, that man came again.

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:55.430
He must like our cakes.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:56.930
Did you talk to him?

00:16:56.930 --> 00:16:57.660
No.

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:02.250
We have nothing more to talk about.

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:05.490
What?

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:07.860
Well, gramps...

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:09.840
How should I say this...

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:14.380
Are you running this cake shop to get the man who kidnapped you?

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:19.600
I can't really explain, but no.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:23.930
So there are things that even you can't explain, huh?

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:25.350
Yeah, there are.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:26.770
I see.

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:28.150
Yeah.

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:30.410
Let's make this a good shop.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.860
I can't explain it well,

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:33.900
but I'll do my best.

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:35.290
Yeah.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:37.910
You did quite well today.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:49.560
Thank you very much for your visit today.

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:52.010
We await your next visit.

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:54.300
Nakai-kun...

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:58.760
So you ended up in a completely standard French confectionery after all.

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:03.720
We really had a hard time because of you.

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:05.440
But...

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:08.600
you're making cakes as good as you did before.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:11.390
See you.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:18.170
Good for you.

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:19.990
Yeah.

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:22.660
O-Ono-san...

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:24.840
Sorry.

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:26.910
I'm relieving my tension...

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:30.190
Can I stay like this for a while?

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:31.080
Yeah.

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:33.530
Thanks.

00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:40.800
So,

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:45.640
well done for making it through our first day at the fair.

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:47.390
Good job.

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:55.270
Boss?

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.700
What's happened all of a sudden?

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:06.870
Well, I thought of trying the cakes you made.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:08.200
Huh?

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.790
You don't have to, since you don't like sweets.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.280
Well,

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:15.210
I'm curious about how well you're doing.

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:18.450
In fact, I'm still an apprentice.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:21.000
This way, sir.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:22.070
G-Gramps.

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:23.970
Quick, go get the dessert.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:24.800
Eh?

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:27.810
You aren't an apprentice anymore.

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:38.690
Here you are.

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:43.910
This is a Cassis dessert he made.

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:47.390
Well then, I'll give it a try.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.000
This tastes very good.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.280
Yes!

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:02.590
Eh?

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:03.860
Eiji.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:10.320
I know what you said last time,
but you can come back if you want to.

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:17.360
Boss.

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:22.340
When I think I'm finally a proper pâtissier,

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:24.350
then I'll come back.

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:28.440
Because I'm already your child.

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:33.240
Are you sure about not going back?

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:33.990
Yeah.

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:37.320
I'll go clean up.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:42.730
Kanda-kun has to leave the dorm at the gym

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:44.880
and is looking for a place to live now.

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.370
Eiji.

00:20:49.190 --> 00:20:52.180
I'll lend you the room upstairs.

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:53.100
Eh?

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:56.350
But you'll have to work harder.

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:58.560
You're a proper pâtissier now.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:00.140
Gramps,

00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:01.980
thanks heaps.

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:04.160
Can't you say, "Thank you very much"?!

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:04.990
Geez.

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:16.960
This time the boss smells very nice.

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.090
I can't stand this.

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:19.530
I want to eat him up.

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:21.920
Help me!
